:19073178\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000142 \"A cell occurring in the peripheral part of the vitreous body of the eye that may be responsible for production of hyaluronic acid and collagen.\")\n5249:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000150 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002530)))\n5264:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000152 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002365)))\n5283:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21907708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30571046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Gastric_chief_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000155 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by a basally located nucleus, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, and large apical secretory granules. It produces and secretes pepsinogen, the inactive precursor of the digestive enzyme pepsin.\")\n5292:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001276))\n5293:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010038))\n5311:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1183/09031936.00146609\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1378/chest.12-2762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28128362\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29874100\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7905712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000158 \"A non-mucous, epithelial secretory cell that is part of the tracheobronchial tree. A club cell has short microvilli but no cilia. A club cell is able to multiply and differentiate into ciliated cells to regenerate the bronchiolar epithelium and it also protects the tracheobronchial epithelium.\")\n5350:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31670611\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000162 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by its pyramidal shape, abundant mitochondria, and a complex network of secretory canaliculi lined with microvilli. It secretes hydrochloric acid into the stomach lumen and produces intrinsic factor, essential for vitamin B12 absorption.\")\n5359:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001276))\n5360:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010038))\n5370:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000163 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0046879 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009)))))\n5371:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000163 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000949))\n5441:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000169 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000164 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000006) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030073)))\n5463:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000171 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002067 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000006)))\n5484:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000173 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000502 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001264)))\n5486:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000173 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000006))\n5503:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000175 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002512))\n5529:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000178 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0005212))\n5561:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000182 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002107))\n5597:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000186 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002384))\n5601:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D032342\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000187 \"A mature contractile cell, commonly known as a myocyte. This cell has as part of its cytoplasm myofibrils organized in various patterns.\")\n5623:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000188 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001134)))\n5694:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000197 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001032) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050906)))\n5766:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000207 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0005725))\n5824:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000214 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002217))\n5842:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000216 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000630 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001343)))\n5889:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000221 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000924))\n5899:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000222 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000926))\n5908:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000223 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000925))\n6068:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_squamous_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000240 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of squamous epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cells. The basal layer is directly attached to the basement membrane and the apical layer consists of flattened squamous cells. This provides a protective barrier, commonly found in areas subject to abrasion, such as the skin, oral cavity, and esophagus.\")\n6070:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000240 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0006915)))\n6075:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_cuboidal_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000241 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of cuboidal epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cuboidal cells forming the apical layer. This provides a protective lining for ducts in large glands, such as sweat glands.\")\n6077:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000241 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010077)))\n6390:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000287 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000210 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000970)))\n6535:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000307 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003126)))\n6592:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000315 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001817))\n6603:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D012629\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19944183\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000317 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a sebaceous gland. This cell produces and secretes sebum, an oily, lipid-rich substance, through holocrine secretion where the entire cell ruptures to release its contents.\")\n6606:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000317 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001821)))\n6656:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000322 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004821)))\n6751:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000336 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000166 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001236)))\n6817:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000345 \"A mesenchymal cell that is part of a small mass of condensed mesenchyme in the enamel organ; it differentiates into the dentin and dental pulp.\")\n6821:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000345 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001763))\n6830:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000346 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000057 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000412)))\n6839:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000347 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001773)))\n6844:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000348 \"A cell that is part of optic choroid.\")\n6846:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000348 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001776)))\n6852:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000349 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000478)))\n6857:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000350 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000349 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010302)))\n6896:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000355 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000048 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001134)))\n6911:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cjm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000358 \"A smooth muscle cell that is part of a sphincter. A sphincter is a typically circular muscle that normally maintains constriction of a natural body passage or orifice and which relaxes as required by normal physiological functioning.\")\n6913:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000358 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004590)))\n6922:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000359 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002049)))\n6931:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000360 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000085))\n6938:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000361 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004734))\n6950:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000362 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0007376)))\n6980:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000366 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000084 from Plant Ontology instead. Male gamete, part of male germ unit.\")\n7025:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:978-0801481253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000372 \"An epidermal cell that is part of a cell cluster organ of the insect integument (such as a sensillum) and that secretes a cuticular specialization that forms a socket around the base of a cuticular specialization produced by a trichogen cell.\")\n7039:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:978-0801481253\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000374 \"An epidermal cell that is part of a cell cluster organ of the insect integument (such as a sensillum) and that secretes a cuticular specialization, often in the form of a hair, bristle, peg or scale. The base of this specialization is often surrounded by a socket produced by a closely associated tormogen cell.\")\n7072:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000379 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001017))\n7092:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/B978-012369493-5.50012-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1017/CBO9780511818202.024\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000382 \"A cell that is part of a scolopidium and surrounds the dendrite of a scolopidial neuron.\")\n7096:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000382 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001038))\n7133:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37894875\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:957445\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000388 \"An elongated fibroblast that is part of a tendon. Its cytoplasm is stretched between the collagen fibres of the tendon, and it possesses a central nucleus with a prominent nucleolus. Tendon cell has a well-developed rough endoplasmic reticulum, and it is responsible for the synthesis and turnover of tendon fibres and ground substance.\")\n7137:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000388 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000057 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000043)))\n7161:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/B978-012369493-5.50008-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000392 \"A hemocyte that synthesizes and secretes melanins as part of the antimicrobial immune response. It is characterized morphologically by crystal inclusions of phenoloxidases in its cytoplasm, hence its name.\")\n7195:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000397 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000045)))\n7265:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000407 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001038))\n7392:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"JB:jb\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000425 \"Forms the terminal part of the cuticle-lined excretory duct of C. elegans.\")\n7417:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/s00412-016-0595-4\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000429 \"A columnar epithelial cell that is part of an insect imaginal disc.\")\n7421:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000429 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000939))\n7472:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000436 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000996))\n7558:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000446 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0011197))\n7575:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000448 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001347))\n7587:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000449 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001348))\n7813:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000477 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000992))\n7861:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000484 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000097 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002384)))\n7872:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000485 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000097 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001961) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002540)))\n7913:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000491 \"This term had an incorrect definition and was overly broad. Consider using 'cytotoxic T cell ; CL:0000910' (in most cases) or another lymphocyte cell type if cytotoxicity is shown to be part of the cell's phenotype in a particular experimental situation.\")\n8014:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000503 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000155))\n8018:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019861\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000504 \"A enteroendocrine cell part of the glands of the gastric mucosa. They produce histamine and peptides such as chromogranins. This cell type respond to gastrin by releasing histamine which acts as a paracrine stimulator of the release of hydrochloric acid from the gastric parietal cells.\")\n8064:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D019879\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29184701\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32308658\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33484640\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000510 \"An epithelial cell found in the basal part of the intestinal glands (crypts of Lieberkuhn) including the appendix. Paneth cells synthesize and secrete lysozyme and cryptdins. Numerous in the deeper parts of the intestinal crypts, particularly in the duodenum, rich in zinc, contain large acidophilic granules, with irregular apical microvilli and prominent membrane-bound vacuoles containing matrix.\")\n8070:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000510 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0011184))\n8095:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000513 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001133) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000746)))\n8193:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000525 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000371))\n8228:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000530 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002240))\n8265:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000535 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002240))\n8267:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000535 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:UBERON_0002342))\n8403:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000548 \"OBSOLETE. A native cell that is part of some Metazoa.\")\n8427:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000550 \"A nucleated, immature erythrocyte in which the nucleus occupies a relatively smaller part of the cell than in its precursor, the basophilic erythroblast. The cytoplasm is beginning to acquire hemoglobin and thus is no longer a purely basophilic, but takes on acidophilic aspects, which becomes progressively more marked as the cell matures. The chromatin of the nucleus is arranged in coarse, deeply staining clumps. This cell is CD71-positive and lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\n8522:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000557 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002371) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000001944) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:PR_000005307) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:PR_000007857) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:CL_4030045 obo:PR_000007858) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001865) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030225) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030851)))\n8572:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000561 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000966))\n8640:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18816864\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000569 \"A mesenchymal cell found in the developing heart and that develops into some part of the heart.  These cells derive from intra- and extra-cardiac sources, including the endocardium, epicardium, neural crest, and second heart field.\")\n8656:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000570 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000710 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001024) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0001820 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009))) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0036161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009)))))\n8658:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000570 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_00