002100 obo:UBERON_0002037)))\n13340:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:mah\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001032 \"Granule cell that is part of the cerebral cortex.\")\n13342:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001032 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000120 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956)))\n13348:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001033 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000120 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002421)))\n13355:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001034 \"'In vitro', translating literally to 'in glass', typically refers to a controlled, often sterile, laboratory setting where cells or other specimens are placed by some agent for the purpose of studying or manipulating them as part of some research investigation. 'In vitro' is intended to contrast with 'native',which refers to cells or other biological entities that are found in a natural setting. It describes unicellular organisms removed from a natural environement and multicellular organism cells removed from an organism, or cells derived in culture from such displaced cells.\")\n13365:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0001035 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001474)))\n13369:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VSAO:curator\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001039 \"Osteoblast that is terminally differentiated, located adjacent to acellular or cellular bone tissue within periosteum, and is capable of mineralizing the matrix.\")\n13382:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001040 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002481))\n13670:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23292121\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23348417\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001065 \"A lymphocyte that lacks characteristic T cell, B cell, myeloid cell, and dendritic cell markers, that functions as part of the innate immune response to produce cytokines and other effector responses.\")\n13729:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0001070 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001347))\n13839:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001200 \"Types of B lineage lymphocytes include B cells and antibody secreting cells (plasmablasts and plasma cells).  Lymphocytes of B cell lineage can be distinguished from those of T cell lineage by their lack of CD3e (as part of the T cell receptor complex).\")\n14583:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002060 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002097))\n14659:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002064 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000622 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001263)))\n14672:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002066 \"A neuroendocrine cell found in the epithelium of the lungs and respiratory tract. This cell type is rounded or elliptical in shape, situated mainly in the basal part of the epithelium; regulates bronchial secretion, smooth muscle contraction, lobular growth, ciliary activity and chemoreception. Cell has an electron-lucent cytoplasm, contains numerous dense-cored vesicles with a clear halo between the core and the limiting membrane.\")\n14741:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002071 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000584 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001278)))\n14779:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15817800\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30291131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37925434\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002075 \"A rare type of columnar epithelial cell that is part of the tracheobronchial epithelium. This cell is characterized by a distinctive tuft of apical microvilli, which extends into the cytoplasm, and a pear-shaped morphology, broad at the base and tapering to a narrow apex. It plays vital roles in chemosensation, producing cytokines like IL-25, and enhancing mucociliary clearance through acetylcholine release to support mucus movement and airway defense.\")\n14784:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002075 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002204 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008397)))\n14822:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002079 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001064) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0015106)))\n14835:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002080 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001263) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0015106)))\n14859:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002082 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000336 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001236) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0048242)))\n14870:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002083 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000336 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001236) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0048243)))\n14896:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0002085 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004670))\n14976:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002092 \"MH consider whether bone marrow cells are bone cells in the structural sense vs. being part of bone organ sense.\")\n14978:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002092 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0001035 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002371)))\n15022:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002096 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000187 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0009966)))\n15034:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002097 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002078 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001235)))\n15058:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002099 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002097 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002053)))\n15345:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0002126 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000799 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(o