 nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\n31679:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n31683:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\n31692:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889))\n31693:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4030007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0007589))\n31702:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030008 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000653 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002120)))\n31707:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23799132\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23897681\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31249312\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030009 \"A brush border cell that is part of segment 1 (S1) of the proximal tubule epithelium, located in the renal cortex.\")\n31711:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4030009 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004196) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005903)))\n31716:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23799132\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23897681\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31249312\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31253652\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030010 \"A brush border cell that is part of segment 2 (S2) of the proximal tubule epithelium, 